WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.370 --> 00:00:14.040
Dear viewers, Venezuela may soon undergo a
historic change.

00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:15.240
“What are we?

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:17.240
Venezuela, what do we want?

00:00:17.240 --> 00:00:18.240
Freedom”.)

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:21.440
“This is a crucial moment for the people
of Venezuela”)

00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:29.009
For the first time, it feels like we’re
on the verge of witnessing the end of Chavez’s

00:00:29.009 --> 00:00:30.009
Bolivarian Revolution.

00:00:30.009 --> 00:00:37.980
“We’re giving our support to President
Guaidó because we don’t agree with what

00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:42.539
is happening in Venezuela, because we’ve
practically had to leave as exiles.

00:00:42.539 --> 00:00:44.980
We want justice and freedom to return.”)

00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:49.550
As you all know, this man, Juan Guaidó, the
President of the Venezuelan National Assembly,

00:00:49.550 --> 00:00:53.079
has been proclaimed interim President of the
country.

00:00:53.079 --> 00:00:59.769
“The time of freedom is getting closer and
closer”)

00:00:59.769 --> 00:01:03.410
And over 50 world leaders along with almost
all Latin American countries have already

00:01:03.410 --> 00:01:05.010
recognized him as such.

00:01:05.010 --> 00:01:08.950
“Guaidó is the person we’re talking to”

00:01:08.950 --> 00:01:17.330
“The Spanish Government announces that it
officially recognizes Mr. Juan Guaidó Márquez

00:01:17.330 --> 00:01:32.760
as President in Charge of Venezuela”

00:01:32.760 --> 00:01:39.780
“Colombia recognizes Juan Guaidó as President
of Venezuela”

00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:45.680
“Juan Guaidó as president in charge”

00:01:45.680 --> 00:02:07.240
“The Parliament voted, we recognize him
as interim president”)

00:02:07.240 --> 00:02:10.940
All this, coupled with the United State’s
recent sanctions which have frozen oil revenues,

00:02:10.940 --> 00:02:17.180
have put the Bolivarian regime in a very tight
spot.

00:02:17.180 --> 00:02:31.550
Dear viewers, the scenario that Nicolás Maduro
now faces is complicated, very complicated.

00:02:31.550 --> 00:02:35.260
For one thing, not only has his authority
been questioned in the global arena, opposition

00:02:35.260 --> 00:02:38.090
from the Venezuelan population is also undeniable.

00:02:38.090 --> 00:02:42.290
Secondly, the country is on the verge of collapsing
as a whole, because it’s about to run out

00:02:42.290 --> 00:02:43.690
of dollars and petrol.

00:02:43.690 --> 00:02:46.500
Yes, petrol, you heard that correctly.

00:02:46.500 --> 00:02:50.510
Up until now, Venezuela has been importing
a significant chunk of its petrol from the

00:02:50.510 --> 00:02:51.510
United States.

00:02:51.510 --> 00:02:56.180
Check this out:

00:02:56.180 --> 00:03:03.939
PDVSA imports 70% of the gasoline the domestic
market consumes.

00:03:03.939 --> 00:03:04.939
El Nacional)

00:03:04.939 --> 00:03:08.920
But of course, now, with a virtually worthless
Venezuelan currency and no ability to buy

00:03:08.920 --> 00:03:10.200
dollars... those days are over.

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:16.519
So the question remains, can a country survive
without petrol and without oil I doubt it.

00:03:16.519 --> 00:03:18.310
And, you know what?

00:03:18.310 --> 00:03:23.570
Nicolás Maduro and his henchmen know this,
they know that their time may be about to

00:03:23.570 --> 00:03:24.969
run out... forever.

00:03:24.969 --> 00:03:27.989
But let’s consider what that would mean
for just a moment.

00:03:27.989 --> 00:03:30.950
More specifically, let’s look at these two
questions:

00:03:30.950 --> 00:03:36.380
One: How has the Chavista regime, now headed
by Nicolás Maduro, survived for so long?

00:03:36.380 --> 00:03:39.569
And, two: Is a peaceful transition possible?

00:03:39.569 --> 00:03:44.890
Folks, the answer to both questions involves
the same characters.

00:03:44.890 --> 00:03:48.560
Listen up.

00:03:48.560 --> 00:03:54.069
(THE BOLIVARIAN GESTAPO)

00:03:54.069 --> 00:04:01.150
Now, let's not fool ourselves, changing Venezuela
is going to be a very, very difficult task.

00:04:01.150 --> 00:04:03.689
Even if Nicolás Maduro were to leave quietly.

00:04:03.689 --> 00:04:08.049
The Bolivarian Revolution has not only plundered
and destroyed the Venezuelan economy, it has

00:04:08.049 --> 00:04:12.219
also created lots of networks and nefarious
interests of all kinds.

00:04:12.219 --> 00:04:19.060
Some of these networks have played a key role
in allowing Nicolás Maduro to remain in power.

00:04:19.060 --> 00:04:24.560
We’re talking mainly about two institutions
which have been essential for the maintenance

00:04:24.560 --> 00:04:26.669
of the entire Chavista regime.

00:04:26.669 --> 00:04:31.160
The first is the regime’s formidable secret
police, the SEBIN, or Bolivarian National

00:04:31.160 --> 00:04:32.380
Intelligence Service.

00:04:32.380 --> 00:04:35.370
The other is FAES, the Special Operations
Forces.

00:04:35.370 --> 00:04:40.289
We’re talking about two organizations that
haven’t hesitated to kidnap, imprison, rob,

00:04:40.289 --> 00:04:45.240
repress and “eliminate” political opponents
and anyone whom the Chavista regime consider

00:04:45.240 --> 00:04:48.669
a threat.

00:04:48.669 --> 00:04:53.530
Two organizations that have become Nicolas
Maduro’s army of personal bodyguards.

00:04:53.530 --> 00:04:58.000
And even if there is a change of government
in Venezuela, they would probably continue

00:04:58.000 --> 00:05:03.370
operating in the shadows, dedicating themselves
to their fields of expertise: robbery, extortion

00:05:03.370 --> 00:05:04.370
and drug trafficking.

00:05:04.370 --> 00:05:05.979
But how did it get to this point?

00:05:05.979 --> 00:05:07.820
How do these organizations work?

00:05:07.820 --> 00:05:10.240
What role do they really play?

00:05:10.240 --> 00:05:15.400
That deserves a closer look.

00:05:15.400 --> 00:05:16.400
.

00:05:16.400 --> 00:05:23.050
Well, first things firstl, we have to acknowledge
that this isn’t at all new.

00:05:23.050 --> 00:05:27.400
Almost all dictatorships have been known to
use armed forces to consolidate their power,

00:05:27.400 --> 00:05:35.310
instil fear of speaking out against the government,
and to get rid of political opponents.

00:05:35.310 --> 00:05:38.780
Throughout the twentieth century perhaps the
three most well-known cases were Mussolini’s

00:05:38.780 --> 00:05:42.870
“OVRA” – an organization that kept an
eye on and actively repressed antifascism,

00:05:42.870 --> 00:05:49.160
Stalin’s “People's Commissariat for internal
affairs” and the Nazi’s Gestapo.

00:05:49.160 --> 00:05:54.919
The chief goal of these organizations was
not so much about maintaining security or

00:05:54.919 --> 00:06:00.909
upholding justice, but about consolidating
power for their respective dictatorial governments.

00:06:00.909 --> 00:06:04.610
Well, Venezuela’s case isn’t any different.

00:06:04.610 --> 00:06:07.639
SEBIN and FAES aim to protect characters such
as Diosdado Cabello:

00:06:07.639 --> 00:06:09.500
“This individual is a drug trafficker.

00:06:09.500 --> 00:06:14.210
I personally don’t pay him much attention
because I don’t know if in a month, in six

00:06:14.210 --> 00:06:16.160
months he’ll be in jail.

00:06:16.160 --> 00:06:18.110
There’s no future for him.)

00:06:18.110 --> 00:06:22.550
And, folks, as the economic crisis grows,
these two armed groups have been stepping

00:06:22.550 --> 00:06:26.410
up their activity.

00:06:26.410 --> 00:06:29.449
We need look no further than January 2019.

00:06:29.449 --> 00:06:33.539
After Juan Guaidó’s declaration as President
and the subsequent public protests calling

00:06:33.539 --> 00:06:37.710
for Nicolás Maduro to step down, Maduro used
these organizations to try to silence the

00:06:37.710 --> 00:06:38.710
protesters.

00:06:38.710 --> 00:06:41.250
And here’s a question for you, Can you guess
how they went about this?

00:06:41.250 --> 00:06:45.479
It’s not so difficult because it’s straight
out of the dictatorship playbook.

00:06:45.479 --> 00:06:49.710
In the first week after Juan Guaidó’s proclamation,
it’s estimated that 35 people were dispatched,

00:06:49.710 --> 00:06:55.890
falling victims to these criminals, and more
than 800 others were arrested.

00:06:55.890 --> 00:07:05.610
(THE REVOLUTION’S “DIRTY WORK”)

00:07:05.610 --> 00:07:10.039
Back in 2015, Nicolas Maduro created the PLO,
the “Operation of the People's Liberation”

00:07:10.039 --> 00:07:14.069
with the supposed objective of combating the
growing violence that the country was experiencing.

00:07:14.069 --> 00:07:18.610
It was a move that would have horrendous results
for Venezuelans:

00:07:18.610 --> 00:07:27.120
You see, between 2015 and 2016, it’s estimated
that there were around 18,000 cases of arbitrary

00:07:27.120 --> 00:07:29.790
arrests, searches without a warrant and even
executions.

00:07:29.790 --> 00:07:34.889
Building on this experience, the regime went
on to create the FAES or “special action

00:07:34.889 --> 00:07:36.629
forces” in 2017.

00:07:36.629 --> 00:07:40.740
This was an intervention group with special
training and very particular procedures.

00:07:40.740 --> 00:07:41.750
Check this out:

00:07:41.750 --> 00:07:46.710
“First, they use military force to take
an area, as if they were an occupying army.

00:07:46.710 --> 00:07:49.479
Then they proceed to “hunt” their objectives.

00:07:49.479 --> 00:07:54.509
This isn’t about citizen security, where
an offender’s actions are prevented or he’s

00:07:54.509 --> 00:07:59.620
arrested within a legal framework, NO, in
their case they understand that they have

00:07:59.620 --> 00:08:04.469
to get rid of “elements” who aren’t
so much people, as enemies of the regime.”

00:08:04.469 --> 00:08:06.430
Keymer Ávila)

00:08:06.430 --> 00:08:12.080
“The FAES work in popular neighborhoods
with officers dressed in black and equipped

00:08:12.080 --> 00:08:14.159
with sophisticated combat equipment.”

00:08:14.159 --> 00:08:19.360
José Vicente Rangel, former Vice President
of the Republic and former Defense Minister.)

00:08:19.360 --> 00:08:29.409
So you could say that the FAES use brutality
and fear as their default techniques.

00:08:29.409 --> 00:08:33.610
And not only do they carry out random acts
of extreme violence, they have also become,

00:08:33.610 --> 00:08:38.860
in many cases, veritable criminal groups that
have turned theft, organized crime and extortion

00:08:38.860 --> 00:08:45.440
into sources of income.

00:08:45.440 --> 00:08:49.240
And to top it off, they act hand in hand with
the so-called “collectives”.

00:08:49.240 --> 00:08:54.010
These are para-police groups, with many local
volunteers amongst their ranks, created, armed

00:08:54.010 --> 00:08:56.120
and financed by the Chavista regime.

00:08:56.120 --> 00:09:00.579
They were first formed back in 2002 with the
idea of controlling neighborhoods at grassroots

00:09:00.579 --> 00:09:01.579
level.

00:09:01.579 --> 00:09:05.060
That way, any Venezuelan who disagreed with
the regime would not only r be controlled

00:09:05.060 --> 00:09:10.530
by the police and the intelligence services
but also by some of their very own neighbors.

00:09:10.530 --> 00:09:13.790
Controlled... and, of course, terrified.

00:09:13.790 --> 00:09:18.950
Because, folks, in many cases these “collectives”
have taken the law into their own hands and

00:09:18.950 --> 00:09:23.570
have e set up their own businesses, which
are also linked to drug trafficking and extortion.

00:09:23.570 --> 00:09:28.100
In return FAES often sets up its operatives
within these “collectives” and their local

00:09:28.100 --> 00:09:29.100
businesses.

00:09:29.100 --> 00:09:32.720
Can you think of another country where the
police act hand in hand with criminal gangs?

00:09:32.720 --> 00:09:35.070
How about: Nicaragua.

00:09:35.070 --> 00:09:36.209
And wouldn’t you know it!

00:09:36.209 --> 00:09:38.399
They are one of Maduro’s allies.

00:09:38.399 --> 00:09:42.640
Meanwhile SEBIN, the powerful Bolivarian National
Intelligence Service created by Hugo Chavez

00:09:42.640 --> 00:09:45.790
in 2010, hasn’t been left out.

00:09:45.790 --> 00:09:52.940
“Venezuela has a set of hidden enemies,
people who act and use public liberties to

00:09:52.940 --> 00:09:59.620
conspire against the republic’s peace and
tranquility.

00:09:59.620 --> 00:10:05.180
And the SEBIN has been an extraordinary instrument
to neutralize them..”)

00:10:05.180 --> 00:10:13.790
The agents of SEBIN, a symbol of the repression
in Venezuela, are in charge of the most delicate

00:10:13.790 --> 00:10:18.339
operations, such as arresting and persecuting
opponents, even if those opponents are Deputies

00:10:18.339 --> 00:10:22.450
of the National Assembly or members of the
Venezuelan Parliament.

00:10:22.450 --> 00:10:28.410
“SEBIN has become one of the symbols of
state terrorism implanted in Venezuela, it’s

00:10:28.410 --> 00:10:33.370
an organization that has developed a policy
of grave human rights violations.”

00:10:33.370 --> 00:10:35.010
Marino Alvarado)

00:10:35.010 --> 00:10:38.680
To this day, both groups operate from the
shadows and with total impunity.

00:10:38.680 --> 00:10:43.500
For example, no one really knows exactly how
many agents work at SEBIN, nor how many people

00:10:43.500 --> 00:10:47.870
have actually been detained, or who is in
charge of the various departments.

00:10:47.870 --> 00:10:52.430
The only thing we know for sure is that SEBIN
is ruled by this man: Manuel Cristopher Figuera;who

00:10:52.430 --> 00:10:58.000
is rumoured to be under the thumb of Tareck
El Aissami, a high-ranking minister in Maduro’s

00:10:58.000 --> 00:10:59.481
government and Vice President of the Economic
Area.

00:10:59.481 --> 00:11:04.160
A guy who, incidentally, is considered a drug
trafficker by the United States.

00:11:04.160 --> 00:11:08.390
We also know that SEBIN operates with such
impunity that it even ignores the Bolivarian

00:11:08.390 --> 00:11:09.730
courts themselves.

00:11:09.730 --> 00:11:11.400
That’s right.

00:11:11.400 --> 00:11:13.910
Let me explain.

00:11:13.910 --> 00:11:18.450
There are numerous documented cases where
political prisoners were ordered to be released

00:11:18.450 --> 00:11:23.110
by the Bolivarian “justice system”, but
they are still in jail because SEBIN simply

00:11:23.110 --> 00:11:24.579
refuses to let them go.

00:11:24.579 --> 00:11:27.130
Dear friends of VisualPolitik, the building
you see in these images is perhaps the best

00:11:27.130 --> 00:11:30.880
proof of the real disaster that Venezuela
has suffered through in the last decades.

00:11:30.880 --> 00:11:31.990
Let me explain.

00:11:31.990 --> 00:11:36.320
This futuristic-looking building that evokes
the Tower of Babel is the Helicoide.

00:11:36.320 --> 00:11:42.500
Construction began in 1956 and it was intended
to house a shopping centre and a luxury hotel.

00:11:42.500 --> 00:11:45.270
These days it’s one of SEBIN’s two main
headquarters.

00:11:45.270 --> 00:11:47.311
This is where they have their holding cells.

00:11:47.311 --> 00:11:51.589
Cells which, as you can imagine, are maintained
in dreadful conditions.

00:11:51.589 --> 00:11:55.790
“The cells have no bathrooms and you aren’t
guaranteed medical attention.

00:11:55.790 --> 00:12:00.120
Prisoners are almost always locked up, it
could take weeks or months to be let out for

00:12:00.120 --> 00:12:01.120
a few minutes.

00:12:01.120 --> 00:12:06.240
I’ll never forget that the inspector who
received me after my arrest told me: “Welcome

00:12:06.240 --> 00:12:07.240
to hell.”

00:12:07.240 --> 00:12:10.690
Vilca Fernández, former candidate for the
National Assembly)

00:12:10.690 --> 00:12:14.920
Once locked up, SEBIN agents charge the families
of the inmates for necessary items such as

00:12:14.920 --> 00:12:15.920
food.

00:12:15.920 --> 00:12:18.790
Of course that money , goes directly into
the agents’ own pockets.

00:12:18.790 --> 00:12:21.110
But let’s get back to the subject at hand.

00:12:21.110 --> 00:12:27.870
Do you know the extent of what these groups
have done in recent years?

00:12:27.870 --> 00:12:34.861
Well, according to information provided by
the Organization of American States’s, we

00:12:34.861 --> 00:12:40.980
could be talking in excess of 8,000 executions,
mainly carried out by these groups.

00:12:40.980 --> 00:12:42.870
And that’s only since 2015.

00:12:42.870 --> 00:12:47.010
And the data from the Venezuelan Violence
Observatory is even worse.

00:12:47.010 --> 00:12:52.190
According to this organization, in 2018 alone,
security forces got rid of more than 7,500

00:12:52.190 --> 00:12:53.470
people.

00:12:53.470 --> 00:13:01.399
Folks, SEBIN and FAES have not only been Nicolas
Maduro’s armed wing, they have also been

00:13:01.399 --> 00:13:03.670
the life support that has kept him in power.

00:13:03.670 --> 00:13:07.580
If the time for change does come, they will
no doubt cause quite a few headaches.

00:13:07.580 --> 00:13:11.579
If these groups already have links with drug
traffickers today, it wouldn’t be at all

00:13:11.579 --> 00:13:15.480
unusual for this to become their main activity
at a later date.

00:13:15.480 --> 00:13:18.529
But we’ll talk about that in another video.

00:13:18.529 --> 00:13:19.529
Now it's your turn.

00:13:19.529 --> 00:13:23.529
Here’s a key question for you: In the interests
of moving forwards, do you think amnesty should

00:13:23.529 --> 00:13:28.630
be given to all the leaders involved in crimes
such as kidnapping, plundering and destroying

00:13:28.630 --> 00:13:29.630
Venezuela?

00:13:29.630 --> 00:13:31.760
Leave your answer in the comments as well
as in the survey.

